a ceremony to mark the departure of more  french troops from northern mali this is  the third military base in the region to  be vacated by french troops during the  last few months  the bases in tassalit and kidal have  already been handed over to malin troops  france has decided to withdraw more than  2 000 of its soldiers from the sahel  region by early next year  but it's not because the so-called war  on terror has been won or domestic peace  has been maintained armed groups linked  to al-qaeda and isil have stepped up  their attacks across the region the  latest of those targeting unpeacekeepers  in northern mali earlier this week  this morning in mali  seven togolese u.n peacekeepers died and  three others were  seriously injured when their vehicle hit  an improvised explosive device in the  bandigyara region of central mali the  peacekeepers were part of a logistics  convoy traveling from dueensa to sivari  interpretations differ as to why france  has decided to reduce its military  footprint in a region that for long  remained part of its strategic presence  in africa outstanding however is the  level of unease between paris and bamako  since the overthrow of mali's  democratically elected president ibrahim  bakar keta in a military coup last  august  france along with the au and other  regional bodies condemned the takeover  of power by force attempts to persuade  the new leaders to restore power to  civilians have failed  so have attempts to speed up a process  that could lead to an election in the  next few months reports the coup leaders  are in secret talks with a russian  private security force known as the  wagner group has worsened political  tensions with france and mali's allies  within the group of five neighboring  countries france began redeploying its  military after a surge of attacks in  mali burkina faso and niger  french troops however continue to  operate in the city of gao one of the  hot spots in northern mali  france says they'll provide support to  you and peacekeepers in the region  two thousand of those peacekeepers  remain in timbuktu after the french  withdrawal  both they and malian troops in the area  are facing frequent attacks by armed  groups after nine years of french and  u.n military intervention the situation  in mali is still as precarious as ever  muhammad
 

